// src/v4/extdeps/languages/lean.dag
//
// Scope: Lean 4 model — direction-agnostic language spec. The PROOF-1
//        prover target: gunbc's structural evidence (A2 termination
//        descent, the U1 algebra-homomorphism chain, cost, effects) is
//        EMITTED as a Lean proof term; Lean's small independently-
//        audited KERNEL checks it (the external trust-discharge for A3).
// Anchor: Lean 4 — the versioned upstream language reference
//         (https://leanprover.github.io/lean4/doc/ ; def / theorem /
//         inductive / termination_by / decreasing_by). The spec is the
//         fidelity authority the worker models against. Per L-2 the
//         SPEC is modeled, NOT Mathlib/the library — a Lean library is
//         just a program in the modeled language = `Node`.
// Why (B-2, side-session 2026-05-15 — operator-ratified): PROOF-1
//   (#3158, merged) framed the capability "no new file" and deferred
//   its prover model to "realized when a lean/coq model lands". THIS
//   is that model. B2-OMNI structurally REQUIRES a LanguageModel file
//   to emit to any target, so PROOF-1's "emit to a lean model" needs
//   exactly this file; adding it is the closed-tree extension the
//   operator ratified (STRUCTURE.md invariant #1). ONE prover first —
//   Lean — scoped to the first theorem class: TERMINATION (A2
//   structural descent ≈ Lean well-founded recursion /
//   `termination_by`/`decreasing_by`). Coq is the DEFERRED
//   second-prover falsification probe ("does the model generalize
//   across provers?") — O(1) per B2-OMNI, added only when a theorem
//   class needs it, same probe posture as L-1/L-3; a future
//   operator-ratified extension, never a silent TODO.
//
// Owns:
//   - Lean 4 grammar (def / theorem / inductive / structure /
//     termination_by / decreasing_by / by-tactic blocks) as
//     declarative production DATA (B2-OMNI generic walker, not
//     per-language procedural code)
//   - the proof-term EMIT direction for PROOF-1: a gunbc evidence
//     `Node` → a Lean term the Lean kernel checks. EXPORT only — the
//     prover kernel-checks, NEVER searches (no-engine + A2 "checker
//     not discoverer"); ungroundable evidence ⇒ fail-closed Diagnostic
//     (inherits gunbc's honesty boundary, never papered over)
//   - first theorem class: termination (A2 DescentEvidence → Lean
//     well-founded recursion). Algebra-law (L7) / cost classes are
//     LATER compositions over the same one U1 carrier, not new
//     subsystems
//   - per-feature C5-fidelity disposition in-model (L-2): proof-
//     irrelevant surface is Declared-normalized, never silently lost
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/algebra.dag (the U1 homomorphism evidence
//     PROOF-1 exports), std/diagnostic.dag (the fail-closed boundary)
//   - cross-ref: DECISIONS.md PROOF-1 (A3 trust-discharge, merged
//     #3158) + L-4 + STRUCTURE.md §7 + L-2 + B2-OMNI
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md PROOF-1 (T-15). Coq is NOT in
// the file tree (deferred second-prover probe — a future
// operator-ratified extension, never a silent TODO).
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the
// immutable contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires
// explicit operator ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.extdeps.languages.lean


import v4.std.integer { Int, UInt }
import v4.std.collection { List }
import v4.std.logic { Bool }
import v4.std.nat { Nat }
import v4.std.node { Symbol }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes
//
// SPEC, NOT MATHLIB (L-2). The carriers below model Lean 4's language
// surface and kernel-checkable proof artifacts: declarations, terms,
// inductives, theorem/proof boundaries, and termination clauses. Mathlib
// declarations are ordinary programs in the modeled language, not
// extdeps vocabulary.
//
// CHECKER, NOT SEARCH ENGINE. PROOF-1 exports gunbc evidence to Lean
// terms; Lean checks those terms. This file does not model tactic search
// as an engine and does not add a theorem-prover subsystem. A tactic
// block that cannot be represented as a kernel-checkable term is outside
// F and must fail closed at the B2-OMNI boundary.
//
// D2 RESOLVER SHAPE. Lean primitive aliases below are D2a(1)
// alias-identity rows to std/ carriers. Algebra inhabitance remains owned
// by std/integer.dag / std/nat.dag / std/logic.dag. D2a(2) grounding-map
// rows are deferred until the shared `GroundingMap` home is pinned. D2a(3)
// operation-semantics rows are Lean-specific only where the spec supplies
// a fact distinct from the std carrier, such as proof irrelevance,
// reduction/checking mode, or theorem export normalization.
//
// SCOPE NEGATIVE. This file is the Lean LanguageModel/prover target for
// the first theorem class, termination. It does not model Coq, SMT-LIB,
// Mathlib APIs, Lake package metadata, editor elaborator UX, or a general
// proof search strategy.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// LeanDeclarationKind — closed Lean declaration categories needed for
// the PROOF-1 termination export slice.
//
// Coproduct dissolution — 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: grammar, emit, and proof-export consumers
//      all dispatch on declaration kind.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: reducing to Symbol would make the closed
//      spec categories stringly and uncheckable.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: external language declaration taxonomy.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: one Lean declaration has one top-level kind.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: declarations have heterogeneous
//      payload/validation rules, not one F<X>.
type LeanDeclarationKind
  = LeanDef
  | LeanTheorem
  | LeanInductive
  | LeanStructure
  | LeanAxiom


// LeanName — opaque qualified name reference. The Symbol is identity,
// not readable spelling; textual pretty-printing is a grounding-map /
// LanguageModel spelling fact.
type LeanName {
  namespace: List<Symbol>
  local: Symbol
}


// LeanBinderInfo — binder visibility in Lean term syntax.
//
// Coproduct dissolution — 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: parser, emitter, and elaboration boundary
//      all consume binder visibility.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: Bool cannot distinguish explicit,
//      implicit, strict implicit, and instance implicit.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: Lean syntax/spec fact.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a binder has one visibility.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: closed nullary alternatives.
type LeanBinderInfo
  = ExplicitBinder
  | ImplicitBinder
  | StrictImplicitBinder
  | InstanceImplicitBinder


type LeanBinder {
  name: LeanName
  type: LeanTerm
  info: LeanBinderInfo
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// LeanTerm — the kernel-level term surface this model needs for
// termination proof export. This is a domain recursive type over Lean
// terms, not a new kernel connective; the universal pivot remains Node.
//
// Coproduct dissolution — 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: type checking, emission, and proof export
//      share this exact term classifier.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: heterogeneous payloads; a flat record
//      would admit invalid mixtures like a lambda with no binder but an
//      application argument.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: Lean term grammar is the external source.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: one term node has one syntactic form.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: heterogeneous constructors.
type LeanTerm
  = LeanSort { level: Symbol }
  | LeanConst { name: LeanName }
  | LeanVar { name: LeanName }
  | LeanApp { function: LeanTerm, argument: LeanTerm }
  | LeanLambda { binder: LeanBinder, body: LeanTerm }
  | LeanForall { binder: LeanBinder, body: LeanTerm }
  | LeanLet { binder: LeanBinder, value: LeanTerm, body: LeanTerm }
  | LeanMatch { scrutinee: LeanTerm, alternatives: List<LeanMatchAlternative> }


type LeanMatchAlternative {
  constructor: LeanName
  binders: List<LeanBinder>
  body: LeanTerm
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Termination export shape. A2 descent evidence maps to Lean's
// `termination_by` / `decreasing_by` clauses; Lean checks the result.
type LeanTerminationMeasure {
  subject: LeanName
  measure: LeanTerm
}


type LeanDecreasingProof {
  proof: LeanTerm
}


type LeanTerminationClause
  = LeanTerminationBy { measure: LeanTerminationMeasure }
  | LeanDecreasingBy { proof: LeanDecreasingProof }


// LeanProofArtifact — the PROOF-1 export unit. The source evidence is a
// Node-side proof artifact read by lenses; this file models the Lean
// target term boundary, not a new gunbc proof system.
type LeanProofArtifact {
  declaration: LeanDeclarationKind
  name: LeanName
  type: LeanTerm
  proof: LeanTerm
  termination: List<LeanTerminationClause>
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// C5 fidelity boundary for Lean. Proof-relevant kernel terms are modeled;
// non-kernel surface conveniences normalize or fail closed.
type LeanFidelityFeature
  = LeanKernelTerm
  | LeanPrettyNameSpelling
  | LeanWhitespaceAndLayout
  | LeanTacticScript
  | LeanElaboratorOnlySyntax
  | LeanUnresolvedUniverseLevel
  | LeanUnsupportedTheoremClass


type LeanFidelityDisposition
  = LeanModeled
  | LeanDeclaredNormalized { feature: LeanFidelityFeature }
  | LeanFailClosed { feature: LeanFidelityFeature }


fn lean_feature_disposition(f: LeanFidelityFeature) -> LeanFidelityDisposition {
  match f {
    LeanKernelTerm => LeanModeled
    LeanPrettyNameSpelling => LeanDeclaredNormalized { feature: LeanPrettyNameSpelling }
    LeanWhitespaceAndLayout => LeanDeclaredNormalized { feature: LeanWhitespaceAndLayout }
    LeanTacticScript => LeanFailClosed { feature: LeanTacticScript }
    LeanElaboratorOnlySyntax => LeanFailClosed { feature: LeanElaboratorOnlySyntax }
    LeanUnresolvedUniverseLevel => LeanFailClosed { feature: LeanUnresolvedUniverseLevel }
    LeanUnsupportedTheoremClass => LeanFailClosed { feature: LeanUnsupportedTheoremClass }
  }
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// D2a(3) Lean operation/proof-checking semantics. These are genuine Lean
// resolver facts; they are not algebra-inhabitance rows.
type LeanReductionSemantics
  = KernelDefinitionalReduction
  | OpaqueAxiomBoundary
  | ProofIrrelevantProposition


type LeanProofCheckSemantics<IRCarrier> {
  reduction: LeanReductionSemantics
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// D2a(1) alias-identity rows. These are Lean's language-level primitive
// names resolved to existing std/ carriers; the algebra flows through
// std/, not through this file.
type LeanBool = Bool
type LeanNat = Nat
type LeanInt = Int
type LeanUInt = UInt


// 🟡 TRACKED-SCAFFOLD — D2a(2) grounding maps and D2a(3) data rows.
//
// D2a(2): `data lean_bool_grounding: GroundingMap<LeanBool> = ...` and
// peers are deferred until the shared `GroundingMap` type has a single
// pinned home. This file must not declare `GroundingMap` locally.
//
// D2a(3): top-level data rows selecting `LeanReductionSemantics` for
// specific exported primitives / theorem artifacts are deferred until the
// shared operation-realization path can validate those rows uniformly.
// The carrier shape above is canonical; individual rows belong to the
// Lean LanguageModel resolver data, not to std/algebra.dag.
